		<unit label="chapter" identifier="28" level="3">Trespasses; Fences</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="5" level="4">No-Fence Law</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>55.1-2819</section_number>
	<catch_line>Lands under quarantine</catch_line>
	<text>
		The boundary line of each lot or tract of land in any county in the Commonwealth that is under quarantine shall be a lawful fence as to any and all domesticated livestock.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 8-885; 1977, c. 624, § 55-315; 2019, c. 712.</history>
</law>
